# <%= projectName %>

A TypeScript AI agent built with the [Strands Agents SDK](https://strandsagents.com).

## Getting Started

### Prerequisites

- Node.js >= <%= nodeVersion %>
- An AWS account with Bedrock access (for the default model provider)

### Setup

1. Install dependencies:

   ```bash
   npm install
   ```

2. Copy the environment file and fill in your credentials:

   ```bash
   cp .env.example .env
   ```

3. Run the agent in development mode:

   ```bash
   npm run dev
   ```

## Scripts

| Command         | Description                                  |
| --------------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| `npm run dev`   | Run the agent in development mode (hot-reload) |
| `npm run build` | Compile TypeScript to JavaScript             |
| `npm start`     | Run the compiled agent in production mode    |
| `npm run lint`  | Lint the source code with ESLint             |
<% if (hasMemory) { %>
## Memory Module

This project includes agent memory support. The memory module provides a local
file-based store for development. See `src/memory/` for the implementation.

To swap the memory provider for production, edit `src/memory/provider.ts` and
replace the local store with a persistent backend (e.g., DynamoDB, Redis).
<% } %>
<% if (hasGuardrails) { %>
## Guardrails Module

This project includes input and output guardrails. Example guardrails are
provided in `src/guardrails/` to demonstrate content validation and response
filtering.

To add custom guardrails, create new files in `src/guardrails/` and register
them in `src/guardrails/index.ts`.
<% } %>
<% if (hasA2A) { %>
## A2A Protocol Module

This project includes [Agent-to-Agent (A2A)](https://github.com/a2aproject/a2a-js)
protocol support. The A2A server exposes your agent for communication with other
A2A-compatible agents.

- Agent card: `src/a2a/agent-card.json`
- Server entry point: `src/a2a/server.ts`

Start the A2A server:

```bash
npx tsx src/a2a/server.ts
```
<% } %>
<% if (hasAgentCore) { %>
## AgentCore Deployment

This project includes AWS AgentCore deployment configuration. See the
`deployment/` directory for Docker and deployment scripts.

### Deploy to AgentCore

1. Ensure you have the AWS CLI configured with appropriate permissions.
2. Build the Docker image:

   ```bash
   docker build -f deployment/Dockerfile -t <%= projectName %> .
   ```

3. Run the deployment script:

   ```bash
   bash deployment/deploy.sh
   ```

See `deployment/deploy.sh` for required AWS permissions and prerequisites.
<% } %>

